<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's monetary base up 2.46 percent.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's monetary base up 2.46 percent.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO, Ecuador 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's monetary base rose 2.46 percent to 2.91 billion sucres ($766 million) in the week ended March 7, the Central Bank said Monday.</p>
<p>In February, the monetary base fell 0.38 percent to 2.84 billion sucres.</p>
<p>The monetary base stood at 3.06 billion sucres at the end of 1996, up from 2.41 billion sucres at the end of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
